WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.260
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.180
Are you scared of wasps?

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.430
You will be if you ever get chased by a swarm
of Asian Giant Hornets.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:21.160
They are the world's largest hornets, at 5
times the size of the european honey bee,

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.240
they are nearly as big as your entire thumb,
with a wingspan bigger than a hummingbird's.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:32.220
Also known as the Japanese Giant Hornet, they're
responsible for around 40 deaths every year

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.220
in Japan.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:37.390
They will swarm and aggressively give chase
if you disturb their nest.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:42.840
A single sting is enough to kill a human,
even if you're not allergic to hornet venom.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:48.870
One victim described the sting as feeling
"like a hot nail being driven into my leg."

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.580
Think giant wasp's are deadly?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.350
How about a "sea wasp", that's the name given
to the Australian Box Jellyfish.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.720
The box jellyfish is the most venomous animal
in the world.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.540
They have up to 60 tentacles, each 4.6 metres
(15 feet) long.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:11.479
Each of it's tentacles has 5,000 stinging
cells and enough venom to kill 60 humans.

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:15.619
It's sting will kill you in minutes, by shutting
down your nervous system.

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:18.600
Most victims don't even make it back to shore.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.920
Scary stuff, but don't be fooled by the Cone
Snail.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:27.030
The cone snail looks innocent with its beautifully
ornate shell, but it's a nasty little bugger.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:33.060
A single drop of venom from this underwater
menace is enough to end 20 human lives.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.930
Inside its shell is a poison dart that will
instantly harpoon you if you pick it up.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:42.639
Once its venom is inside you, it will quickly
paralyse your entire body then you have about

00:01:42.639 --> 00:01:45.830
2 hours to live; there is no anti venom.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:49.829
Cone snails are found in the oceans of tropical
countries such as Brazil.

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:55.759
A fear of spiders is extremely commonplace,
but arachnophobics can relax, because they

00:01:55.759 --> 00:02:01.329
may look creepy, but the fact is, an extremely
small percentage of spider species actually

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:04.279
carry venom that is lethal to humans.

00:02:04.279 --> 00:02:09.840
Even the infamous Black Widow's deadliness
is a bit of a myth, Black Widow spiders aren't

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:15.500
aggressive and very rarely bite, but when
they do the dose of toxins they inject is

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.750
usually not fatal to humans.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:23.080
However there is one spider you should worry
about, more than any other.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:28.080
The Amazon Rainforest is home to the world's
most dangerous spider, the Brazilian Wandering

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.080
Spider.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.360
It's awfully aggressive and intensely venomous.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:37.330
Even though they're smaller than most spider
species they're not afraid of humans.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:43.290
Luckily they only inject a dose of venom lethal
to humans 40% of the time, the rest of the

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.670
time you will just feel immense pain.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:51.750
But these little horrors have another rather
humorous but unfortunate side effect.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:57.360
Males bitten by the Wandering Spider will
be afflicted with a prolonged erection.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.800
The spider's venom has been called "natural
Viagra".

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.420
They're all terrifying animals, but for sheer
number of kills none of these killers come

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:09.650
close to the biggest mass murderer of all,
the mosquito.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:15.840
Mosquitos are responsible for between 2 to
3 million human deaths every year, mostly

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.840
in Africa.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.390
They're bites can transfer parasites that
carry malaria.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:27.651
But which animal, if it were you vs. them,
one to one would guarantee your death, if

00:03:27.651 --> 00:03:28.810
it attacks.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.950
The prize goes to the brown bear.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:40.600
Weighing in at 635 kg or 1,400 lbs the grizzly
bear would be your most formidable opponent.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.750
It can kill you with a single swipe of it's
paw.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.380
There's no use running, they're much faster
than you.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:49.170
Brown bears can reach speeds of 30 miles per
hour.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:58.540
Runnersworld.com calculated you would need
a head start of 2,146 metres to outrun a brown

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.150
bear if it chased you.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.050
That's about 21 football pitches.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:07.090
And don't think you can escape up a tree,
or dive into the nearest lake, bears are exceptional

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.460
swimmers and tree climbers.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.390
If a brown bear decide's you're it's breakfast,
you're it's breakfast.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:17.760
Luckily for us, they don't attack humans often,
especially not groups, attacks on groups of

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.430
more than 3 are virtually unheard of.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:23.600
So what truly is the most dangerous animal?

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:37.130
Well if there's one animal I wouldn't want
to get into a fight with, it's the brown bear.

